{"name":"Friendly Fairway","hex":"#3f663e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"friendly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Generally warm, approachable and easy to relate with in character.","Inviting, characteristic of friendliness."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A game which is of no consequence in terms of ranking, betting, etc.","A person or entity on the same side as one's own in a conflict."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/friendly"},{"term":"fairway","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The area between the tee and the green, where the grass is cut short.","Any tract of land free from obstacles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fairway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fairway (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Fairway (1925–1948) was a British Thoroughbred racehorse and sire. Fairway was the best horse of his generation in Britain at two, three and four years old, winning the St Leger Stakes, the Champion Stakes (twice) and the Eclipse Stakes. He retired as a five-year-old in 1930 and went on to become a successful and influential sire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Fairway_%28horse%29.jpg/330px-Fairway_%28horse%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairway_(horse)","wikidata":"Q5430908"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Edward_George_Villiers_Stanley%2C_17th_Earl_of_Derby_by_Sir_William_Orpen.jpg/500px-Edward_George_Villiers_Stanley%2C_17th_Earl_of_Derby_by_Sir_William_Orpen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Edward_George_Villiers_Stanley%2C_17th_Earl_of_Derby_by_Sir_William_Orpen.jpg/1280px-Edward_George_Villiers_Stanley%2C_17th_Earl_of_Derby_by_Sir_William_Orpen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn